Sets the unit both for both command data such as command speed and for actual data such as response speed.",162,
7,26,RTEX warning setup of continuous com. error,"Generates RTEX continuous communication error warning when the number of continuous errors reaches the setting of this parameter.
When the setting value is 0, this function is disabled and no warning is issued.",210,
7,27,RTEX warning setup of cumulative com. error,"Generates RTEX accumulated communication error warning when the number of accumulated errors reaches the setting of this parameter.
When the setting value is 0, this function is disabled and no warning is generated.",215,
7,28,RTEX update counter warning setup,"When the number of continuous updates of Update_Counter has not reached the value set by this parameter, RTEX_Update_Counter error warning is generated.
When the setting value is 0, this function is disabled and no warning is generated.",236,
7,29,RTEX monitor selection 1,Select the monitor type of Response_data1.,42,
7,30,RTEX monitor selection 2,Select the monitor type of Response_data2 when non-cyclic command = 0h.,71,
7,31,RTEX monitor selection 3,Select the monitor type of Response_data3 when non-cyclic command = 0h.,71,
7,32,RTEX monitor selection 4,Select the monitor type of Sub_Response_data1 when 32byte mode or sub command = 0h.,83,
7,33,RTEX monitor selection 5,Select the monitor type of Sub_Response_data2 when 32byte mode.,63,
7,34,RTEX monitor selection 6,Select the monitor type of Sub_Response_data3 when 32byte mode.,63,
7,35,RTEX command setup 1,Set up Command_data3 with non-cyclic command.,45,
7,36,RTEX command setup 2,Set up Sub_Command_data2 with sub command.,42,
7,37,RTEX command setup 3,Set up Sub_Command_data3 with sub command.,42,
7,38,RTEX_Update_Counter error protection setup,"If the Update_Counter exceeds the setup value for this parameter and is not updated correctly,
 Err86.2(RTEX_Update_Counter error protection) will be activated.",160,
7,39,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
7,40,RTEX function extension setup 4,Sets each functions by bit unit.,32,
7,41,RTEX function extension setup 5,Sets each functions by bit unit.,32,
7,42,Not used,,0,
7,43,Magnet pole position estimation completion output setup,"Set up the pit arrangement for outputting magnet pole position estimation completion output (CS_Complete) to byte 3 for the RTEX status.
Setting with this parameter will be prioritized (supersede setting with Pr7.40-bit1).",222,
8,0,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
8,1,Profile linear acceleration ,Set up acceleration of profile positioning operation.,53,
8,2,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
8,3,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
8,4,Profile linear deceleration ,Set up deceleration of profile positioning operation and during Smooth_Stop.,76,
8,5,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
8,6,Not used,,0,
8,7,Not used,,0,
8,8,Not used,,0,
8,9,Not used,,0,
8,10,Profile distance after position latched,Set up the distance of travel upon detection of latch signal input position during external input positioning.,110,
8,11,Not used,,0,
8,12,Profile homing mode,Set up direction of return to home position.,44,
8,13,Profile homing speed 1,"Sets the operation speed during return to home: operation speed after completion of near the origin input turned OFF - ON - OFF and before detection of latch signal.
Note) The max value is limited to the motor max speed by the internal process.",244,
8,14,Profile homing speed 2,"Specifies a velocity for low-speed operation during profile home position return.
Specify a minimum speed to decrease detection error.
Unit is specified with Pr7.25 (RTEX velocity unit setting).
Maximum velocity is internally limited using Pr9.10.",247,
8,15,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
9,0,Motor type selection,Select the type of a motor that will be connected.,50,
9,1,Number of scale pulses per rotation,Set the number of pulses of the feedback scale per revolution.,62,
9,2,Magnet pole pitch,Sets up the pitch of magnetic poles.,36,
9,3,Pole logarithm per rotation,Set up the pole logarithm per motor rotation for the motor.,59,
9,4,Motor inertia,Set up the motor inertia.,25,
9,5,Rated motor torque,Set up the rated torque for the motor.,38,
9,6,Rated effective motor current,Set up the rated effective current for the motor.,49,
9,7,Maximum instantaneous motor current,Set up the maximum instantaneous current for the motor.,55,
9,8,Motor phase inductance,Set up the phase inductance for the motor.,42,
9,9,Motor phase resistance,Set up the phase resistance for the motor.,42,
9,10,Maximum over-speed level,Set up the maximum over-speed for the motor.,44,
9,11,Carrier frequency selection,"Select the carrier frequency.
0: 6 kHz 1: 12 kHz",48,
9,12,Automatic current response adjustment,Set up the criteria for current response for the automatic setup of Pr9.13(Proportional current gain) and Pr9.14(Integral current gain).,136,
9,13,Proportional current gain,Set up the proportional current gain.,37,
9,14,Integral current gain,Set up the integral current gain.,33,
9,15,Not used,,0,
9,16,Not used,,0,
9,17,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
9,18,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
9,19,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
9,20,Magnet pole detection scheme selection,Select the detection scheme for magnet pole position.,53,
9,21,CS phase setup,Set up the phase difference between the induced voltage of the motor and the CS signal.,87,
9,22,Magnet pole position estimation torque command time,Set up the command torque time for magnet pole position estimation.,67,
9,23,Magnet pole position estimation command torque,Set up the command torque for magnet pole position estimation.,62,
9,24,Magnet pole position estimation zero travel pulse width setup,Set up the zero travel pulse width for magnet pole position estimation.,71,
9,25,Number of pulses for magnet pole position estimation motor stop judgment,Set up the number of pulses for motor stop judgment for magnet pole position estimation.,88,
9,26,Time for magnet pole position estimation motor stop judgment,Set up the motor stop judgment time for magnet pole position estimation.,72,
9,27,Time for magnet pole position estimation motor stop limitation,Set up the motor stop limitation time for magnet pole position estimation.,74,
9,28,Magnet pole position estimation torque command filter,Set up the time constant for filter respective to the command torque for magnet pole position estimation.,105,
9,29,Overload protection timing characteristic selection,"Select the overload protection timing characteristic from eight types of characteristics.
0 : Standard",102,
9,30,Number of pulses per magnet pole,"Linear motor information can be set in pulses, which is valid for linear-type settings.
This parameter cannot be used at the same time with Pr9.02(Magnet pole pitch).
Use either of these parameters for setting.",210,
9,31,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.¡£,15,
9,32,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
9,33,For manufacturer's use,100 Please fix.,15,
9,34,For manufacturer's use,0 Please fix.,13,
9,35,Torque saturation error protection frequency,"If torque saturated is continued during a preset frequency, Err16.1(torque saturation protection) will be activated.
If the setup value is 0, this function is disabled and an alarm will not be activated.",203,
